---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const contactEmail = "tymurbogach@gmail.com";
const updatedAt = "October 12, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for LazyTripZ and JobPilot services operated by Tymur Bogach."
>
  <article class="mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl py-6 laptop:py-12 laptop-scaled:py-12">
    <header class="mb-10 border-b border-[var(--border)] pb-8">
      <p class="font-hud mb-3 text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.35em] text-[var(--foreground-faint)] uppercase">
        Homelab services
      </p>
      <h1 class="mb-4 text-4xl leading-tight font-bold text-[var(--foreground)] mobile:text-5xl">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="m-0 text-sm text-[var(--foreground-faint)]">
        Last updated: {updatedAt}
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-[0.95rem] leading-7 text-[var(--muted-foreground)] mobile:text-base">
      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">
          Who operates these services
        </h2>
        <p>
          Tymur Bogach operates LazyTripZ and JobPilot. These services use the
          Homelab Google OAuth project. For privacy questions or data deletion
          requests, email
          <a
            class="font-medium text-[var(--accent)] underline underline-offset-4"
            href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}
          >
            {contactEmail}
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">
          Data used by LazyTripZ
        </h2>
        <p>
          LazyTripZ uses Google Sign-In to authenticate users. It receives your
          Google account identifier, name, email address, and profile picture.
          It uses this data to create and secure your account. LazyTripZ also
          stores travel information that you submit to the service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">
          Data used by JobPilot
        </h2>
        <p>
          JobPilot requests read-only access to Gmail after you connect an
          account. It reads recent message metadata to identify job-related
          messages. This data can include the sender, subject, date, message and
          thread identifiers, and a short message snippet. JobPilot does not
          send, edit, or delete your Gmail messages.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">
          How Google user data is handled
        </h2>
        <p>
          Google account data is used only to provide the features described in
          this policy. OAuth tokens are encrypted before storage. The services
          do not sell Google user data, use it for advertising, or share it with
          unrelated third parties.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          The use and transfer of information received from Google APIs follows
          the
          <a
            class="font-medium text-[var(--accent)] underline underline-offset-4"
            href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Google API Services User Data Policy
          </a>
          , including its Limited Use requirements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">
          Storage and security
        </h2>
        <p>
          The services run on private, self-hosted infrastructure. Access is
          restricted to the service operator. Reasonable technical safeguards
          protect stored data, but no internet service can guarantee absolute
          security.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">
          Retention and deletion
        </h2>
        <p>
          Data is kept only while it supports an active account or the service's
          stated purpose. Disconnecting Gmail stops future access through
          JobPilot. Previously imported message metadata can remain until it is
          deleted. You can request deletion of your account, OAuth connection,
          and stored service data by emailing
          <a
            class="font-medium text-[var(--accent)] underline underline-offset-4"
            href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}
          >
            {contactEmail}
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">
          Policy changes
        </h2>
        <p>
          This page will show material changes to this policy. The date at the
          top shows the latest revision.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
